Negative control for the picker being a CHECKBOX list (`R7-3`).

Takes the checkbox off the package's checkable menu item and leaves the bare
tick it used to draw: an entry that is on carries a glyph, an entry that is off
carries nothing at all, so the menu reads as a list of words rather than a list
of controls and there is no box to aim at. Every behaviour survives — the same
roles, the same `aria-checked`, the same keyboard, the same emit — which is the
point: the defect is what the entry IS, not what it does.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the column-picker spec's control case — an unchecked entry draws no
checkbox, so the entries are not controls.

